# Who may do what on the broker. A node's login is its address, `<site>/<subsystem>/<node>`
# (e.g. `sh1/rf/rf-north`), and it may write only under nodes/<its own login>/. Nobody but the
# gateway reads.
#
# The gateway's login (MQTT_USERNAME in .env; "gateway" here) reads everything under nodes/.
user gateway
topic read nodes/#

# Every login: write under nodes/<login>/ and nowhere else. %u is the login's name, so the topic's
# three levels under nodes/ (site, subsystem, node) are the login itself: the gateway takes the
# site from them. A node id may be `*` (the subsystem's node-less events), which is a plain
# character in a topic and in a login, not a wildcard.
pattern write nodes/%u/#
